2. (noun) a severe shortage of food (as through crop failure) resulting in violent hunger and starvation and death1. (verb) be hungry; go without food — "Let's eat--I'm starving!"
2. (verb) deprive of food — "They starved the prisoners"
3. (verb) die of food deprivation — "The political prisoners starved to death"1. (verb) be hungry; go without food — "Let's eat--I'm starving!"
2. (verb) deprive of food — "They starved the prisoners"
3. (verb) die of food deprivation — "The political prisoners starved to death"
4. (adjective) extremely hungry — "they were tired and famished for food and sleep"1. (noun) a state of extreme hunger resulting from lack of essential nutrients over a prolonged period1. (noun) a histamine blocker (trade name Pepcid) used to treat peptic ulcers and gastritis and esophageal reflux1. (adjective) widely known and esteemed — "a famous actor"1. (noun) a widely known person — "he was a baseball celebrity"1. (adverb) in a manner or to an extent that is well known — "in his famously anecdotal style"
